<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1914 CE – 1922 CE · capital Cairo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Egypt as a British protectorate during and after the First World War, under sultans of Muhammad Ali's line, ended by the 1919 revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ended Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in December 1914, deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-ii-of-egypt">Khedive Abbas II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khedivate-of-egypt">Khedivate of Egypt</a> and declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. His uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-kamel-of-egypt">Hussein Kamel</a> took the title of sultan to mark the break from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> was a major British base for campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellespont">Dardanelles</a>, under martial law. Peasants were conscripted into the Egyptian Labour Corps and crops requisitioned, fuelling resentment. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-kamel-of-egypt">Hussein Kamel</a> died in 1917 and was succeeded by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuad-i-of-egypt">Fuad</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1919 the British exile of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saad-zaghloul">Saad Zaghloul</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wafd-party">Wafd</a> delegation sparked a nationwide revolution. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> unilaterally declared Egyptian independence in February 1922 with reserved powers, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuad-i-of-egypt">Fuad</a> became king of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-egypt">Kingdom of Egypt</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Egypt" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Converted to svg by Daniel78 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Egypt_(1882%E2%80%931922).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1914 CE – 1922 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cairo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hussein Kamel, Fuad I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Egyptian Sultanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=sultanate-of-egypt" aria-label="Sultanate of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5491 1081 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5811 1337L5811 1337M5811 1337L4997 651M5811 1337L5811 1337"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M4997 651h0M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5811 1337h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cairo. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=sultanate-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
